    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12927" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dē-lingo</span></b> , linxi,
		ĕre, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v. a., to lick, lick off</i> or <i>up</i> (very rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cochleare plenum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					3, 22 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">leo puerum delinxit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lampr. Diad. 5, § 6</span></i>
			.—Prov.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">salem,</span>”
				i. e. <i>to have a meagre diet</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					Curc. 4, 4, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. Pers. 3, 3, 25</span></i>.</div>
